  "query": [
   "(query ;; The two puzzle questions are \"who drinks water?\" and \"who owns the ;; zebra?\" — a Nationality, not a House (who, not where). The goal ;; binds the located house, then joins through the shared house to ;; nation-loc so ?who_water / ?who_zebra carry the answer. The goal is ;; projection-only: it cuts each state of R down to its rows and ;; decides nothing about which states are in R, so the extra conjuncts ;; don't gate the search; they let the answer renderer report \"the ;; Norwegian drinks the water\". A query has no mode: what it asks of R ;; is the command's question (`ein solve`, `--single`, `ein test`). :goal (and (drink-loc Water ?h_water) (nation-loc ?who_water ?h_water) (pet-loc Zebra ?h_zebra) (nation-loc ?who_zebra ?h_zebra)) ;; :goal-text renders the headline NL result from the bound goal vars ;; (the rule/relation `:why` `{?var}` engine). This — not any hardcoded ;; verb table — is what prints \"The Norwegian drinks…\" on the solve table. :goal-text \"The {?who_water} drinks water in {?h_water}; the {?who_zebra} owns zebra in {?h_zebra}\")"
